iPhoneDuo epsilon board patch for UniXNU/UniXNU@21d683dff6 (UniXNULib).
Applied by firmware/scripts/build-fd-in-container.sh to the build-time copy of
UniXNUPkg; the UniXNU checkout itself is never modified.

Review finding M1 (data safety):
- Config discovery only reads \EFI\UniXNU\unixnu.toml from the volume whose
  device path starts with the EpsilonPayloadDxe vendor node
  (5AEDCA82-BD6F-4986-BA69-3B08EEC1F803). Any other FAT volume, including the
  Windows ESP, is skipped. With no payload volume the built-in configuration
  is used (actions + removable-media loaders, upstream behaviour).
- Every [[block_slice]] is refused with a config error (a slice is a Block I/O
  view onto a named GPT partition of the internal UFS disk).

Base file SHA-256 (upstream Config.c):
c070b2eb1c4922df345a2f830c5f2c420bafd11dde759fee2d2ce4f3be3923c5

Host build only. Not booted on hardware.

--- a/package/UniXNUPkg/Library/UniXNULib/Config.c
+++ b/package/UniXNUPkg/Library/UniXNULib/Config.c
@@ -1429,6 +1429,18 @@
   }
 
   List = TomlGet (Root, "block_slice");
+
+  //
+  // iPhoneDuo epsilon board patch: a slice is a Block I/O view onto a named
+  // GPT partition of the internal UFS disk (Slice.c), and a writable one
+  // forwards WriteBlocks to it. The epsilon GPT layout (Android + DuoWOA) is
+  // not verified, so every slice is refused.
+  //
+  if ((List != NULL) && (List->Child != NULL)) {
+    ConfigError (Config, "block_slice is disabled on epsilon (line %u)", (UINT32)List->Child->Line);
+    List = NULL;
+  }
